{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "פן תעזוב את הלוי", :translit "pen ta'azov et ha-levi", :gloss "lest you forsake the Levite"} {:he "כי ירחיב", :translit "ki yarchiv", :gloss "when He expands"} {:he "מתן אדם ירחיב לו", :translit "matan adam yarchiv lo", :gloss "a person's giving expands for him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "smikhut (juxtaposition): adjacent verses linked for drash"}], :frame {:text "The principle expressed by the phrase מתן אדם ירחיב לו appears in BT Bava Batra 10a in the name of Rabbi Elazar, and in BT Ta'anit 9a as מתן אדם מרחיב לו, both citing Proverbs 11:24 as prooftext. Ba'al HaTurim applies this principle via the juxtaposition of Deuteronomy 12:19–20, reading the verb ירחיב in verse 20 as an allusion to the talmudic saying about generosity.", :sources ["Bava Batra 10a" "Ta'anit 9a" "Proverbs 11:24" "Deuteronomy 12:19" "Deuteronomy 12:20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "smikhut (juxtaposition): adjacent verses linked for drash", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:13.534239561Z", :model "glm-5.2"}